//
// Why fitted rather than derived: only 20 of the 154 chains are built from eq and hue
// alone, which map exactly. The rest use colorbalance, curves or colorchannelmixer, and
// a curve is non-linear while a colour matrix is linear - so there is no exact mapping
// to derive. What there IS is a nearest one, and it can be found by optimisation and
// then checked rather than assumed.
//
// Each grade was rendered through real ffmpeg on three portraits at different
// exposures, and brightness/contrast/saturate/hue-rotate/sepia were fitted to minimise
// mean absolute error against it. The CSS functions are implemented from the W3C
// filter-effects matrices, which is what Android's ColorMatrixColorFilter applies - so
// the simulation is of the real thing, not of an idea of it.
//
